Theorem L-2: Lattice join associativity

  Preconditions:
    - a, b, c are AimsState elements per the canonical proof notation
      sec-Per-Dimension-Symbol-Set
    - join is the product-lattice componentwise join per Annex E §AIMS + sec-1.8 L-2

  Soundness property:
    Forall a, b, c in AimsState. join(join(a, b), c) = join(a, join(b, c))

  Proof obligation:
    Componentwise per-dimension finite enumeration over the 7 carriers
    proves dim_join_d associativity on every (x, y, z) triple in the
    carrier cubed. Product-lattice associativity follows by the
    componentwise-lift lemma: if every dimension's join is associative,
    the product join is associative.

    Per-dimension triple counts (|carrier| ^ 3):
      Access 2^3 = 8 triples
      Consumption 4^3 = 64 triples
      Cardinality 3^3 = 27 triples
      Uniqueness 3^3 = 27 triples
      Locality 5^3 = 125 triples
      Shape 5^3 = 125 triples
      Effect 8^3 = 512 triples

    Per-dimension argument:
      Access / Consumption / Cardinality / Uniqueness / Locality:
        max on a totally ordered carrier; max is associative because
        max(max(x, y), z) = max(x, max(y, z)) = the maximum of the
        3-element set {x, y, z} (the max function over a finite chain
        is independent of nesting order — it selects the chain-greatest
        element regardless of how the binary max calls are bracketed).
      Shape (flat lattice with Phi absorbing):
        join is a meet with Phi as absorbing top; case enumeration:
        all three equal -> all bracketings return that value;
        any two unequal -> any bracketing introducing Phi propagates
        Phi through subsequent joins (Phi absorbs); each of the 3
        bracketing orders produces the same value. Per-case discharge
        over the 5^3 = 125 triples confirms left == right.
      Effect (componentwise OR on 3-bit flag product):
        OR on Bool is associative; per-flag associativity composes
        componentwise.

    Lift to product:
      join(join(a, b), c) = (dim_join_d(dim_join_d(a_d, b_d), c_d))_d
                          = (dim_join_d(a_d, dim_join_d(b_d, c_d)))_d
                            (per-dim L-2)
                          = join(a, join(b, c))

    Sentinel handling: SCALAR pre-filtered per L-9; FRESH /
    CONSERVATIVE / ALL / NONE are concrete 7-tuples obeying
    componentwise associativity.

    Engines dispatched:
      lattice (per-dimension finite enumeration discharge per
        section_02::verify_l2_associativity)
      monotonicity (validates the per-dimension joins used in L-2 are
        the same primitives whose monotonicity L-6 covers)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: sec-02 lattice engine discharges L-2 via per-dimension finite enumeration of associativity triples
